    "text": "The slum streets channel you the same way they did before—leaning brick, shared load, thin light—but this time you are not finding the trail for the first time. You are walking it with the disturbance already named in your head, your plate confirming what memory already sketched.\r\n\r\nChemical runoff still threads toward the tenements by the old cistern ring. The soil reads spent—almost nothing left—yet that secondary signature holds: small, steady, someone's fuel paying for a private circle in a place where private fuel is its own kind of vow.\r\n\r\nThe path returns you to the crumbling tenement and the basement door: crude bonding paste, a simple lock circle, Freehand work—rough but functional. Someone with genuine skill who doesn't want visitors. The purifier's echo lives behind that threshold; the district's larger arithmetic waits beyond it.",
